-- title:
--   Toric point map: injective homomorphism, image the toric m-torsion
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ lies in `A.nonunits`, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be a level datum for $(p, M, H)$ over $A$ — a morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,A \to$ `base p` extending the generic point, together with a scheme over `base p` carrying a relative group law and identifications of its generic- and special-fibre points with $J_H(M/p)$ at the induced level and with the degree-zero divisor class group of the function field of the reduction — and let $O$ be a $\Gamma_H(M)$ Néron object at $p$ over $\Lambda$, i.e. a smooth separated group scheme $g \colon G \to$ `base p` with commutative relative group law, Hecke correspondences, an identification `O.pts` of $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular curve $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the generic-fibre points of $g$, a toric rank $t =$ `O.toricRank` and toric lifts. Let $m > 0$. Writing $\iota_m(\chi) =$ `O.toricPoint m hm χ` for the point of $J_H(M)$ attached to an $A$-algebra map $\chi \colon A[(\mathbb{Z}/m)^t] \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, obtained by composing the corresponding $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $\mu_{m,A}^{t}$ with the toric lift, base-changing to the generic point and transporting through `O.pts`, the theorem asserts four things: $\iota_m$ is additive for the convolution product on characters (phrased via `WithConv`), $\iota_m$ is injective, an element of $J_H(M)$ lies in the subgroup `O.toricPts m` (the subgroup generated by the image of $\iota_m$) precisely when it is of the form $\iota_m(\chi)$, and `O.toricPts m` has exactly $m^{t}$ elements.
--
--   This identifies the toric $m$-torsion of a Néron object of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ dividing the level with the character group $\mathrm{Hom}((\mathbb{Z}/m)^{t}, \mu_m(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})) \cong \mu_m(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})^{t}$, the group of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of the $m$-torsion of the toric part of the special fibre lifted to the generic fibre. It is used downstream to show that toric points have degree zero, to produce an isomorphism of `O.toricPts` with the character lattice modulo $m$ when the special fibre points are of node-unit type, and to pin down the toric lift up to a bialgebra automorphism; these are the ingredients of the analysis of the $p$-adic monodromy pairing behind level lowering.
